# Linux System Health Monitor

A beginner-friendly Linux system monitoring project built using Bash scripting.

## About the Project

The Linux System Health Monitor is a command-line automation tool designed to collect basic Linux system information and generate timestamped health reports.

This project is being developed to understand Bash scripting, Linux administration, system monitoring and automation.

## Technologies Used

- Ubuntu Linux
- GNU Bash
- Linux command-line utilities
- Git and GitHub

## Current Features

- Collects hostname information.
- Identifies the current logged-in user.
- Records the current date and time.
- Collects system uptime and load averages.
- Generates timestamped text reports.

## Planned Features

- CPU utilization monitoring.
- RAM usage monitoring.
- Disk space monitoring.
- Top CPU- and memory-consuming processes.
- Network connectivity checks.
- System health status and alerts.

